const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:"cat > /tmp/monthly-design-luna.md <<'EOF'
# Monthly declaration updates: candidate design

## Problem

`/rankings` already has a bulk declaration read path, canonical alias-group funder identities, service registration in `AppState`, and same-origin SvelteKit API loaders. It is a poor semantic fit for monthly updates: its repository is scoped by a single lower bound, and its model/service deliberately aggregate financial totals. A monthly updates page needs the full set of MPs and non-individual canonical funder groups that occur in declarations registered during one UTC month, across every category, with distinct declaration counts and no amount data. The existing domain convention classifies every `FunderKind` except `Individual` as a company. Existing profile links are `/members/{id}` and `/funders/{uuid}`.

## Usage (caller's view)

The page loader gets a typed current-month snapshot through the existing server-only API boundary:

```ts
// frontend/src/routes/updates/+page.server.ts
const updates = await loadMonthlyUpdates(fetch, request.signal, origin);
return { updates, error: null };
```

The page renders two complete lists and profile links from the response; it does no filtering, counting, or ordering:

```svelte
{#each data.updates.members as member}
  <a href={`/members/${member.id}`}>{member.name}</a>
  <span>{member.declarationCount}</span>
{/each}
{#each data.updates.companies as company}
  <a href={`/funders/${company.id}`}>{company.name}</a>
  <span>{company.declarationCount}</span>
{/each}
```

The Rust caller is one operation, with time supplied internally so callers cannot accidentally choose local-time month boundaries:

```rust
let updates: MonthlyUpdates = state.monthly_updates_service.current_month().await?;
```

A repository fake or focused domain test can request a deterministic window via the private/pure summarizer rather than changing the public current-month operation.

## Shape

### Data structures

```rust
/// Exact UTC interval [start, end) for one calendar month.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct UtcMonth { start: DateTime<Utc>, end: DateTime<Utc> }
impl UtcMonth {
    pub fn containing(at: DateTime<Utc>) -> Self; // calendar month, UTC, end is next month start
    pub const fn start(self) -> DateTime<Utc>;
    pub const fn end(self) -> DateTime<Utc>;
}

pub struct MonthlyMember { pub id: MemberId, pub name: String,
    pub latest_registration: DateTime<Utc>, pub declaration_count: u32 }
pub struct MonthlyCompany { pub id: FunderId, pub name: String,
    pub latest_registration: DateTime<Utc>, pub declaration_count: u32 }
pub struct MonthlyUpdates { pub month_start: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub members: Vec<MonthlyMember>, pub companies: Vec<MonthlyCompany> }

/// One persisted declaration plus its member and zero or more distinct canonical
/// non-individual funders represented by entries in that declaration.
pub(crate) struct MonthlyDeclarationFact {
    declaration_id: i64, registered_at: DateTime<Utc>, member: RankedMember,
    companies: Vec<RankedFunder>,
}
```

`MonthlyDeclarationFact` should use a dedicated minimal member identity rather than `RankedMember` if that would import ranking-only fields; it must not contain amounts, currencies, or category-specific fields. Canonical companies can be formed with the same SQL alias-group joins and `FunderKind` parser already used by `outbound/rankings.rs`. One fact row per declaration is preferred: the SQL query returns declaration/member plus canonical funder columns; the adapter groups rows by declaration and de-duplicates canonical funder IDs before emitting facts. It includes declarations with no matching funders via left joins.

### Module map and signatures

- `domain/models/monthly_updates.rs`: `UtcMonth`, output records, and crate-private repository fact.
- `domain/repositories/monthly_updates.rs`: persistence contract.
- `domain/services/monthly_updates.rs`: `MonthlyUpdatesService::current_month`, captures one `Utc::now()` and derives one `UtcMonth`; pure `summarize(facts, window)` owns distinct counting and ordering.
- `outbound/monthly_updates.rs`: one `sqlx::query!` bulk query using `registration_date >= start AND registration_date < end`, all declaration categories, canonical alias root and preferred group name; no amount columns.
- `inbound/http/handlers/monthly_updates.rs`: response mapping only; `GET /updates` returns month start, members, companies and counts.
- `AppState` and `routes`: add one `MonthlyUpdatesService` generic and service field, register the handler, construct it beside rankings in `serve_exposed`.
- `frontend/src/lib/server/monthly-updates.ts`: fetch and validate response at server boundary. `frontend/src/routes/updates/+page.server.ts` calls it; `+page.svelte` renders rows with profile URLs. The existing `AppShell` provides common shell; adding a new footer/navigation link is a separate visible-copy/navigation decision and isn't required for the route itself.

```rust
pub trait MonthlyUpdatesRepo: Clone + Send + Sync + 'static {
    fn declarations(&self, month: UtcMonth)
      -> impl Future<Output = Result<Vec<MonthlyDeclarationFact>, MonthlyUpdatesError>> + Send;
}
pub trait MonthlyUpdatesService: Clone + Send + Sync + 'static {
    fn current_month(&self)
      -> impl Future<Output = Result<MonthlyUpdates, MonthlyUpdatesError>> + Send;
}
fn summarize(facts: Vec<MonthlyDeclarationFact>, month: UtcMonth) -> MonthlyUpdates;
```

The loader validates UUID/member ID shapes, strings, non-negative safe integer declaration counts, and an ISO month start, matching the existing `loadRankings` boundary style. The client receives serializable data only. The endpoint's response uses snake_case JSON as the rankings endpoint does; server parsing maps to camelCase page types.

### Ownership and invariants

`UtcMonth` owns UTC calendar arithmetic and the half-open interval. The repository owns storage decoding and one bulk snapshot read, not business counts. The monthly service owns output aggregation: each MP count increments once for each declaration; each canonical funder group count increments at most once per declaration even if that group's funder appears on several entries; each declaration contributes across every category. Each result's `latest_registration` is the maximum timestamp among included appearances. Sort descending by that timestamp, then ascending by normalized display name, then typed ID for a total deterministic order. The `FunderKind` enum remains the sole kind vocabulary; the `kind != Individual` rule can be expressed by a method on that enum to avoid a copied variant allowlist. A single `now` read means a request spanning a UTC month boundary still uses one consistent month.

There are no amount/currency properties in fact or output types, so financial aggregation cannot leak into this feature. `MonthlyUpdates` contains every qualifying member/company, not a top-N. Parse database identities at the adapter boundary and retain `MemberId`/`FunderId` internally. HTTP DTOs stay private to the handler.

### Interface depth

The public service exposes one operation and hides clock capture, UTC month bounds, canonical-group deduplication, per-declaration counting, and stable sorting. The repo exposes one bulk read taking a validated month. The handler and Svelte loader are thin transport boundaries; no caller coordinates query/aggregation phases.

## Synthesis decision

Single-runner candidate. This shape deliberately gives monthly updates a dedicated query/service rather than stretching ranking contracts: the two use different time windows and output invariants, and rankings' exact-total model would carry irrelevant financial policy into this page.

## Tradeoffs accepted

- We accept one more service and repository module in exchange for keeping monthly semantics and the no-financial-data contract explicit.
- We accept returning one fact per declaration with its companies in order to make declaration-level distinct counts obvious and keep repeated entry rows from inflating counts.
- We accept recalculating the current month per request in exchange for making `/updates` current by definition; each request still captures one clock instant.
- We accept natural-person profile identifiers and canonical funder group identifiers as returned by current profile endpoints, preserving existing profile navigation.

## Alternatives considered

- Reuse `RankingsService::rankings()` and filter its companies and members in Svelte: loses declarations outside donation/support categories for funder inclusion, returns only top ten rows, lacks monthly bounds and entails totals. It exposes ranking policy to the page and cannot satisfy completeness.
- Add a second operation and time-window mode to rankings: modestly less module surface, but callers inherit a mixed financial/ranking/monthly interface and future changes risk coupling two unrelated aggregation policies. This hides less complexity from callers than a focused monthly service.
- Have SQL return final counts and sort order: makes the query compact, but moves declaration-level distinctness and temporal sorting policy into persistence, and makes pure domain behavior less directly testable. SQL should bound/select facts; the service should own domain counting.

## Implementation reconciliation

No implementation performed. Preserve this contract unless a concrete repository/schema constraint requires a deviation; record any accepted change and its acceptance source here.

## Open questions and risks

- Does the product intend `/updates` to be reachable through a new persistent navigation link? The current `AppShell` only has footer links, so the route can exist without adding visible copy or changing shared navigation.
- Does the product define “latest” as most recent registration date (as proposed) or should ordering be by first occurrence/name? The proposed newest-first order uses the registration timestamp already governing inclusion.
- The backend currently parses all `FunderKind` values strictly. A newly introduced stored kind will fail the monthly endpoint until the canonical enum is updated; this is consistent with the current rankings path.

## Test plan

- `UtcMonth::containing` at UTC month start, final representable instant before next month, December-to-January rollover, and timestamps with non-UTC offsets normalized to UTC.
- Repository SQLx integration test verifies start is included, next-month start excluded, null registration excluded, all categories included, declarations with no funding entries retain the member, alias members resolve to preferred canonical company group, and duplicate entries for one group in one declaration are collapsed.
- Service tests verify every member/company is returned, member count is declarations not entries, company count is distinct declaration/group pairs, a group repeated in multiple categories counts once per declaration, all non-individual kinds qualify and Individual does not, newest timestamp is retained, ties sort by name then ID, and no amount/currency fields exist in output.
- Handler integration test verifies `/updates` envelope, month start, counts, profile IDs, and error mapping.
- Frontend parser tests reject malformed IDs/counts/date; page test verifies all rows render with `/members/{id}` and `/funders/{id}` links and has no truncation/top-ten behavior.

## Next implementation step

Add the typed UTC month and monthly update service/repository contracts, then implement the bounded SQLx query and pure count/order summarizer against them.
